[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2455493939","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98768#issuecomment-2455493939","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98768","id":2455493939,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SW90z","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-04T19:08:25Z","updated_at":"2024-11-04T19:08:25Z","body":"I'll do a test to see how it affects Web builds size. Could be interesting if it reduces size, less if it bloats the builds.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2455493939/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2457945856","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98768#issuecomment-2457945856","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98768","id":2457945856,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SgUcA","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-05T19:02:30Z","updated_at":"2024-11-05T19:02:30Z","body":"> I'll do a test to see how it affects Web builds size. Could be interesting if it reduces size, less if it bloats the builds.\r\n\r\nFrom my test, it doesn't really seem to affect build size at all. So I'm all for the PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2457945856/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2458048457","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98768#issuecomment-2458048457","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98768","id":2458048457,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SgtfJ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-05T20:01:24Z","updated_at":"2024-11-05T20:01:24Z","body":"I'm not sure about this. I think moving more towards `constexpr` could be helpful, but we should be adding it in response to an actual need of the project. We shouldn't be adding in new C++ features just because. A large reason why we stick to older C++ is because it can be read and understood by a much wider range of people. \r\n\r\nOur best practices for contributors highlight that [\"the problem must come before the solution\"](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/best_practices_for_engine_contributors.html#the-problem-always-comes-first) and [\"the problem must exist in the first place\"](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/best_practices_for_engine_contributors.html#to-solve-the-problem-it-has-to-exist-in-the-first-place) In other words, we shouldn't be anticipating problems and then trying to solve them. \r\n\r\nI think this PR is well-intentioned and is doing something that might be helpful, but I don't think it is solving any problem and is trying to get ahead of something that might be a problem in the future. \r\n\r\nSimilarly with [[nodiscard]], by adding it indiscriminately, we are adding noise to the git repo, adding compile time to CI and local projects, and complicating the codebase for other contributors. But we aren't solving any problems. [[nodiscard]] is helpful in some cases (which is why we use it in some cases), but we should only be applying it when we need it. Its not something we should just add it everywhere just because.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2458048457/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2458165207","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98768#issuecomment-2458165207","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98768","id":2458165207,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ShJ_X","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-05T21:15:46Z","updated_at":"2024-11-05T21:15:46Z","body":"I can concede the `[[nodiscard]]` additions might be superflous and probably are too noisy. I'm fine removing those\r\n\r\n`constexpr` is a bit trickier. If it was like the original proposal, where I tried overhauling the style & syntax of several functions to accomodate it, then I'd be more inclined to agree; that's part of the reason I turned the original proposal into a draft. However, the more focused nature of this and the dependancy PR makes changes that *can* be impacted by them much more obvious to integrate. The file changes in the dependancy were a result of unused variables now being discovered, and the test changes here were a result of being able to evaluate test conditions at compile-time. I'd argue both of these, while niche, *are* benefits of `constexpr` that the repo is taking immediate use of\r\n\r\nThis might not be a direct response to a \"problem\" needing to be solved, but I wouldn't say that it's trying to be that either. This feels more in-line with codestyle/QOL PRs, where the benefits come from the repo itself having more functionality/readability. `constexpr` is mercifully compact compared to a lot of other modern C++ features, being LESS verbose than current implementations on occasion (`static _FORCE_INLINE_` → `constexpr`), so it generally stands alone in terms of the kind of stuff I'd actively *want* to change to more modern C++ (second only to `type_traits`)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2458165207/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2460838866","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98768#issuecomment-2460838866","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98768","id":2460838866,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SrWvS","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-06T21:40:27Z","updated_at":"2024-11-06T21:40:27Z","body":"> Our best practices for contributors highlight that [\"the problem must come before the solution\"](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/best_practices_for_engine_contributors.html#the-problem-always-comes-first) and [\"the problem must exist in the first place\"](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/best_practices_for_engine_contributors.html#to-solve-the-problem-it-has-to-exist-in-the-first-place) In other words, we shouldn't be anticipating problems and then trying to solve them.\r\n\r\nWhile I agree with the premise, I think we should be cautious applying this principle relative to code style changes. Especially if code changes simplify the code.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2460838866/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2727470388","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98768#issuecomment-2727470388","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98768","id":2727470388,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ikeU0","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-16T14:27:42Z","updated_at":"2025-03-16T14:27:42Z","body":"Now that #92059 is closed, this functionally supersedes that PR; renamed the title/commit message to include constructors as well","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2727470388/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]